  "result": "I wrote `tests/unit/intervals.test.ts` with 15 tests and ran `npx vitest run`. **11 pass and 4 fail.** All four failures come from one bug in `src/intervals.ts`, which I didn't change, as you asked.\n\n**The bug:** the doc comment says the function merges blocks that \"overlap or touch\", and that no two blocks in the result touch. But `src/intervals.ts:18` checks `start < last[1]`, so blocks that only touch, like `[1, 2]` and `[2, 3]`, are left separate. Changing the check to `start <= last[1]` should make all four tests pass.\n\n**Failing tests (all about touching blocks):**\n- `merges intervals that touch at an endpoint`: `[[1,2],[2,3]]` comes back unmerged.\n- `merges a chain of touching intervals`\n- `handles zero-length intervals`: `[3,3]` isn't merged into `[1,3]`.\n- `produces output where no two intervals touch or overlap`\n\n**Passing tests:** empty input, a single block, separate blocks, overlapping blocks, a block inside another, unsorted input, duplicates, negative numbers, the input not being changed, and the result not reusing the input's arrays.\n\nI wrote the tests to match the doc comment rather than the current behaviour. If touching blocks are meant to stay separate, the doc comment is what's wrong, and those four tests would need their expected values changed.",
